{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMpxyWsCVcCSGa65C7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Connecting now works end to end against a local fake of Intervals.icu. I have not tried it against the real service: I had no client credentials and didn't contact Intervals. The first real check is an authorize URL from a real account.\n\n**Causes** (details in `ANSWER.md`):\n\n1. **Connect failed for everyone.** The button was a plain `<a href>` to a GET endpoint. Navigations don't send the `Authorization` header, so it always got a 401.\n2. **Duplicate scopes.** `SCOPES` listed `ACTIVITY` and `CALENDAR` twice. Intervals rejects that before the consent screen. The calendar scope went in on 2026-10-02, which is why the paste-the-link workaround stopped working.\n3. **\"Reconnect after an hour.\"** Intervals returns no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token`. The server filled in a made-up one-hour expiry, and the refresher then marked the connection expired without contacting Intervals. Rivera's token was never revoked.\n4. **Token exchange and state.** The exchange sent `grant_type` and `redirect_uri`, which the endpoint doesn't take. The state had no `purpose` claim. Nothing stopped a reconnect from attaching a different Intervals account.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `config.py`: scopes are `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`, each area once. Refresh config is removed.\n- `server.py`: init is an authenticated POST that returns `{authorize_url}`. State is an HS256 JWT with `purpose` and a 15-minute TTL. The exchange sends only `client_id`, `client_secret` and `code`. There is no expiry and no refresh. A 401 from Intervals marks the connection `reconnect`. The callback refuses a different athlete id on reconnect.\n- `static/app.js`: Connect is a button that POSTs, then navigates to the returned URL. The `reconnect` status shows a message.\n- `test_connect.py` (new): 8 tests against a local fake, all passing with `python3 -m unittest -v test_connect`.\n\n**Decisions and gaps:**\n- I left out `SETTINGS:WRITE` from the guide's scope example, since the app never writes settings.\n- The logs show a generic `invalid_request` for the duplicated URL, not the \"Duplicate scope\" text the guide mentions. The fix is the same either way.\n- Encryption at rest is not implemented. Tokens sit in memory as plaintext. This needs doing before the database move.\n- Restarting the server drops all connections, so athletes will need to reconnect after a restart.\n- Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2186,"cache_read_input_tokens":59530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2186},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41dddc1f-8fb6-4204-aee7-77c938fb5338","uuid":"273913d2-fcc0-409b-9f90-2f7d839b139d","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:30:47.964Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMpxdS7S3hm9VSyZwUp"}
